IMPORT prelude

-- Supreme Court (General Civil Procedure) Rules 2025 (Vic) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions of the prelude (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY,
-- DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. It carries the counting rules of Order 3, by which every period in the
-- Rules "shall be calculated" (r 3.01(1)):
--   r 3.01(2): a period "to begin on, or to be calculated from, a day or event" excludes that day;
--   r 3.01(3): a period "to end on, or to be calculated to, a day or event" includes that day;
--   r 3.01(4): "a period of 5 days or less" excludes any day the office of the Court is closed;
--   r 3.01(5): where "the last day for doing any act" is a day the office is closed, the act "may be done on the next day
--              the office is open";
--   r 3.04(1): "the period from 24 December to 9 January next following shall be excluded, unless the Court otherwise
--              orders";
--   r 3.08:    the office is closed on Saturdays, Sundays and every general public holiday.
-- Public holidays are not computed (the Public Holidays Act 1993 is not deposited): where they matter the question asks
-- whether the day is one (forks F2 and F3 in NOTES.md).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Supreme Court
-- (General Civil Procedure) Rules 2025, S.R. No. 85/2025, Version No. 003 (1 January 2026), not the authorised version.
